## 4. Stories to edit

### Edit 143505, Set up CI/CD pipeline for Pod 3's repo

Title, replace with: Set up the pipelines for the mapper library and the Bank Wire Rail II API repositories

Points: 5. Sprint: 26.4.4. Assignee: Tejaswi.

Description, replace with:
Both repositories now exist in cof-primary: the mapper library (bank-wire-object-mapper) and the service (bank-wire-rail-ii-api), both registered under the PIE ASV for now. The service repository was generated by the DevNav Hub Fargate API template with a Bogiefile that drives the OnePipeline build, scan and deploy stages, but the wizard left the secrets, PagerDuty and Splunk entries empty, so the shift-left checks fail until they are filled. The library has no pipeline yet. This story makes both pipelines run green on a pull request: the library builds with JDK 21, runs its tests and publishes a versioned artifact to the artifact repository that the service can depend on; the service builds, passes the code-quality and security scans, builds its container image and deploys to the dev environment; and the deployment gates for each environment are configured. The pull-request check that requires the Jira ID in the title is confirmed on both repositories.

Acceptance criteria, replace with:

- [ ] Library pipeline builds with JDK 21, runs the unit tests and publishes a versioned artifact that the service resolves as a dependency
- [ ] Service pipeline builds, scans and produces the container image on every pull request
- [ ] Bogiefile entries left empty by the wizard are filled: secrets references, PagerDuty service, Splunk logging
- [ ] Code-quality and security gates pass, with the coverage gate configured
- [ ] Service deploys to the dev environment from the pipeline and the health check passes
- [ ] Deployment gates and approvals are configured per environment and documented in the repository README
- [ ] Pull-request check for the Jira ID in the title is confirmed on both repositories

### Edit 143504, Provisioning for submit OPF

Title, replace with: Provision the dev environment and secrets for the Bank Wire Rail II service

Points: 5. Sprint: 26.4.4. Assignee: Kaushik P.

Description, replace with:
The service runs on Fargate in the entpay dev account under the PIE ASV. This story provisions what the service needs to run there, through the pipeline's infrastructure modules rather than by hand: the Fargate service and task definition, the task role with least-privilege policies, the security group and load balancer, the VPC endpoints for the AWS services it uses, and the outbound route through the enterprise proxy with no direct egress. It creates the secrets the service reads at startup in the enterprise secrets store: the Exchange client credentials for the OPF API sandbox, the encryption secret for the enterprise libraries and the Splunk token, with the secret identifier passed to the service as configuration and the task role allowed to read only those secrets. It records the resulting names, accounts and access steps in the repository runbook so the QA environment can be provisioned the same way later. DynamoDB is provisioned by its own story under Capability 10.

Acceptance criteria, replace with:

- [ ] Fargate service, task definition, task role, security group and load balancer provisioned in the dev account through the pipeline
- [ ] VPC endpoints and the proxy route configured; outbound calls leave only through the enterprise proxy
- [ ] Secrets created in the enterprise secrets store for the OPF API sandbox credentials, the encryption secret and the Splunk token
- [ ] Service reads the secrets at startup through the secret identifier in its configuration; no plaintext credential in the repository or the Bogiefile
- [ ] Task role can read only the service's own secrets
- [ ] Deployed service answers its health check in dev
- [ ] Runbook in the repository lists the resources, accounts, secret names and the steps to repeat for QA

### Edit 143506, Confirm test data / UAT sandbox access for OPF API calls

Title, replace with: Assemble the test data set for the Wire Rail II conversion and submission

Points: 3. Sprint: 26.4.5. Assignee: Vasanth.

Description, replace with:
Sandbox access itself is done (the Code Connect application and credentials exist) and the first accepted call against the sandbox is tracked under Capability 2. What is missing is a shared, versioned test data set that the mapper tests, the WireMock stub, the QA tests and the UAT end-to-end test all use. This story collects representative PayX payment objects for the wire types in scope (customer credit transfer, financial institution transfer, drawdown), including tokenised fields as PayX delivers them, pairs each with the expected pain.001 output and the FIS sample request and responses, adds negative cases that exercise the known rejections, and stores the set in the repository with a short guide on how to use and extend it. No production data is used.

Acceptance criteria, replace with:

- [ ] Payment-object samples exist for each wire type in scope, with tokenised fields as PayX delivers them
- [ ] Each sample has its expected pain.001 output and the matching FIS sample request and response
- [ ] Negative samples cover the known rejection cases and the failure responses FIS provides
- [ ] Test data set is versioned in the repository and used by the unit tests and the WireMock stub
- [ ] Guide in the repository explains the cases and how to add one
- [ ] No production data in the set

