## 5. New story

**Story: Repository conventions, local developer setup and the team context repo**
Points: 3
Sprint: 26.4.3
Assignee: Vasanth

Description

The two repositories exist but have no working conventions yet, and the team context repo that drives the morning plan and the story drafting lacks the design records. This story sets up both repositories the same way: a development branch that pull requests target, feature branches per story, branch protection with a required review and the Jira ID check on the pull-request title, a pull-request template, code owners, and a README that gets a new developer from a fresh laptop to a local run of the service container against the WireMock stub with JDK 21. It moves the prototype code into the service repository on its first feature branch so the merge story can start from there. It also adds the confirmed architecture decision records and, when published, the product requirement documents to the team context repo so stories can be drafted from them.

Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Development branch and branch protection with a required review are configured on both repositories
- [ ] Pull-request template and code owners are in place; the Jira ID check on the pull-request title is confirmed
- [ ] README takes a developer from a fresh laptop to a local run of the service against the WireMock stub with JDK 21
- [ ] Prototype code is on a feature branch in the service repository with a pull request open against development
- [ ] Confirmed architecture decision records are in the team context repo; product requirement documents are added when published

